
==================== 0. Starting point: destination has version 1 ====================

$ rclone sync data/sync-src :s3:site -v --stats 0
2026/11/02 10:24:48 INFO  : S3 bucket site: Bucket "site" created with ACL ""
2026/11/02 10:24:48 INFO  : pages/about.html: Copied (new)
2026/11/02 10:24:48 INFO  : pages/pricing.html: Copied (new)
2026/11/02 10:24:48 INFO  : pages/index.html: Copied (new)
2026/11/02 10:24:48 INFO  : assets/logo.svg: Copied (new)
# someone uploads a file straight to the destination (not in the source)

$ echo "manual upload" | rclone rcat :s3:site/assets/hand-uploaded.pdf

==================== 1. Source moves on to version 2 ====================

$ echo "home v2 - new hero section" > data/sync-src/pages/index.html          # modified

$ rm data/sync-src/pages/pricing.html                                         # deleted

$ mv data/sync-src/pages/about.html data/sync-src/pages/about-us.html         # renamed

$ echo "careers v1" > data/sync-src/pages/careers.html                        # new

$ rclone tree data/sync-src
/
├── assets
│   └── logo.svg
└── pages
    ├── about-us.html
    ├── careers.html
    └── index.html

2 directories, 4 files

==================== 2. What differs? (read-only) ====================

$ rclone check data/sync-src :s3:site --combined - 2>/dev/null   # = same  * differ  + only src  - only dst
- assets/hand-uploaded.pdf
= assets/logo.svg
+ pages/about-us.html
- pages/about.html
+ pages/careers.html
- pages/pricing.html
* pages/index.html
(exit code 1)

==================== 3. --dry-run: what would sync do? ====================

$ rclone sync data/sync-src :s3:site --dry-run 2>&1 | grep -E "Skipped|Deleted:|Transferred:"
2026/11/02 10:24:49 NOTICE: pages/about-us.html: Skipped copy as --dry-run is set (size 9)
2026/11/02 10:24:49 NOTICE: pages/careers.html: Skipped copy as --dry-run is set (size 11)
2026/11/02 10:24:49 NOTICE: pages/index.html: Skipped copy as --dry-run is set (size 27)
2026/11/02 10:24:49 NOTICE: pages/about.html: Skipped delete as --dry-run is set (size 9)
2026/11/02 10:24:49 NOTICE: pages/pricing.html: Skipped delete as --dry-run is set (size 11)
2026/11/02 10:24:49 NOTICE: assets/hand-uploaded.pdf: Skipped delete as --dry-run is set (size 14)
Transferred:   	         47 B / 47 B, 100%, 0 B/s, ETA -
Deleted:                3 (files), 0 (dirs), 34 B (freed)
Transferred:            3 / 3, 100%
# sync would DELETE pricing.html, about.html (renames look like delete + new) AND hand-uploaded.pdf

==================== 4. Sync, keeping everything it replaces or deletes ====================
# --backup-dir moves deleted/overwritten objects aside instead of destroying them (server-side, no re-upload)

$ rclone sync data/sync-src :s3:site --backup-dir :s3:site-trash/$(date +%F) -v --stats 0
2026/11/02 10:24:49 INFO  : S3 bucket site-trash path 2026-11-02: Bucket "site-trash" created with ACL ""
2026/11/02 10:24:49 INFO  : pages/careers.html: Copied (new)
2026/11/02 10:24:49 INFO  : pages/about-us.html: Copied (new)
2026/11/02 10:24:49 INFO  : pages/index.html: Copied (server-side copy)
2026/11/02 10:24:49 INFO  : pages/index.html: Deleted
2026/11/02 10:24:49 INFO  : pages/index.html: Copied (new)
2026/11/02 10:24:49 INFO  : pages/about.html: Copied (server-side copy)
2026/11/02 10:24:49 INFO  : pages/pricing.html: Copied (server-side copy)
2026/11/02 10:24:49 INFO  : assets/hand-uploaded.pdf: Copied (server-side copy)
2026/11/02 10:24:49 INFO  : pages/about.html: Deleted
2026/11/02 10:24:49 INFO  : pages/about.html: Moved into backup dir
2026/11/02 10:24:49 INFO  : pages/pricing.html: Deleted
2026/11/02 10:24:49 INFO  : pages/pricing.html: Moved into backup dir
2026/11/02 10:24:49 INFO  : assets/hand-uploaded.pdf: Deleted
2026/11/02 10:24:49 INFO  : assets/hand-uploaded.pdf: Moved into backup dir

$ rclone tree :s3:site
/
├── assets
│   └── logo.svg
└── pages
    ├── about-us.html
    ├── careers.html
    └── index.html

2 directories, 4 files

$ rclone tree :s3:site-trash     # nothing lost: old versions + the manual upload are recoverable
/
└── 2026-11-02
    ├── assets
    │   └── hand-uploaded.pdf
    └── pages
        ├── about.html
        ├── index.html
        └── pricing.html

3 directories, 4 files

$ rclone cat :s3:site-trash/$(date +%F)/pages/index.html   # the v1 page
home v1

==================== 5. Verify ====================

$ rclone check data/sync-src :s3:site
2026/11/02 10:24:50 NOTICE: S3 bucket site: 0 differences found
2026/11/02 10:24:50 NOTICE: S3 bucket site: 4 matching files
# --download compares actual bytes (for backends without a usable hash)

$ rclone check data/sync-src :s3:site --download
2026/11/02 10:24:50 NOTICE: S3 bucket site: 0 differences found
2026/11/02 10:24:50 NOTICE: S3 bucket site: 4 matching files

==================== 6. Why sync is dangerous ====================
# mistake 1: an empty or wrong source (failed mount, typo, unset variable) = delete everything at the destination

$ mkdir -p data/empty-dir

$ rclone sync data/empty-dir :s3:site --dry-run 2>&1 | grep -E "Skipped delete|Deleted:"
2026/11/02 10:24:50 NOTICE: pages/about-us.html: Skipped delete as --dry-run is set (size 9)
2026/11/02 10:24:50 NOTICE: pages/index.html: Skipped delete as --dry-run is set (size 27)
2026/11/02 10:24:50 NOTICE: pages/careers.html: Skipped delete as --dry-run is set (size 11)
2026/11/02 10:24:50 NOTICE: assets/logo.svg: Skipped delete as --dry-run is set (size 8)
Deleted:                4 (files), 0 (dirs), 55 B (freed)
# guard rail: --max-delete aborts once more than N deletes would happen

$ rclone sync data/empty-dir :s3:site --max-delete 2 -v --stats 0 2>&1 | grep -E "Deleted|ERROR|NOTICE|error" | head -6
2026/11/02 10:24:50 ERROR : pages/index.html: Got fatal error on delete: --max-delete threshold reached
2026/11/02 10:24:50 ERROR : assets/logo.svg: Got fatal error on delete: --max-delete threshold reached
2026/11/02 10:24:50 INFO  : pages/careers.html: Deleted
2026/11/02 10:24:50 INFO  : pages/about-us.html: Deleted
2026/11/02 10:24:50 ERROR : Cancelling sync due to fatal error: failed to delete 2 files
2026/11/02 10:24:50 ERROR : S3 bucket site: not deleting directories as there were IO errors

$ rclone ls :s3:site
        8 assets/logo.svg
       27 pages/index.html
# the abort stopped further deletes, but up to N files may already be gone; --dry-run first is the real protection

$ rclone sync data/sync-src :s3:site -v --stats 0   # restore
2026/11/02 10:24:51 INFO  : pages/careers.html: Copied (new)
2026/11/02 10:24:51 INFO  : pages/about-us.html: Copied (new)
# mistake 2: swapped arguments make the DESTINATION the truth and wipe the source's new work:

$ echo "blog draft, not uploaded yet" > data/sync-src/pages/blog.html

$ rclone sync :s3:site data/sync-src --dry-run 2>&1 | grep -E "Skipped|Deleted:"
2026/11/02 10:24:51 NOTICE: pages/blog.html: Skipped delete as --dry-run is set (size 29)
Deleted:                1 (files), 0 (dirs), 29 B (freed)
# the brand-new local draft would be deleted from the SOURCE. copy would never do this.
# mistake 3: --delete-excluded with a filter deletes every destination file the filter excludes

==================== 7. Safe habits ====================
# use copy unless deletions are really wanted; always --dry-run a new sync first
# --backup-dir (or bucket versioning) so a bad sync is recoverable; --max-delete as a tripwire
# in scripts, refuse to sync from an empty source and quote paths so an unset variable can't become '/'
